  "worked_solution": "Given that $u\u22a5v$ and $u\u22a5w$, we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v=0 \\\\ u\\cdot w=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's consider the first equation $u\\cdot v=0.$ Calculating the dot product in terms of $a$ and $b$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & =0 \\\\ -3\\cdot 3+a\\cdot 4+b\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 1 & =0 \\\\ -9+4a+b-4 & =0 \\\\ 4a+b & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, for the second equation $u\\cdot w=0$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot w & =0 \\\\ -3\\cdot 1+a\\cdot 1+b\\cdot (-3)-4\\cdot (-4) & =0 \\\\ -3+a-3b+16 & =0 \\\\ a-3b & =-13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to find the values of $a$ and $b$, we need to solve the system\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}4a+b=13 \\\\ a-3b=-13\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the first equation by $3$ and adding the result to the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}13a=26\\,\u27f9\\,a=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $a=2$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(2)+b & =13 \\\\ 8+b & =13 \\\\ b & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have that\n\n$$\na+b=2+5=7.\n$$",
